From a711a0f90420ff7afeff9174192181ad2c118b67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tad <tad.keller@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:46:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] ipa: softisp: Add contrast detection autofocus

Add an Af algorithm that drives a voice coil motor lens through
V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE using the focus measure of the statistics. A scan
steps the lens from the infinity end of its range, stops once the contrast
has dropped well past a peak, and moves the lens to the peak, interpolated
by a parabola through its neighbours. It implements AfModeManual
(LensPosition), AfModeAuto (AfTrigger) and AfModeContinuous, which rescans
when the contrast changes and settles again, and can be paused (AfPause).
The scan range, the infinity and macro positions and the step come from the
tuning file.

The IPA gets the lens controls at init and emits setLensControls, which the
simple pipeline handler applies to the sensor's focus lens right away.
